webauthn — third-party attribution
==================================

This file carries a CONDITION, added 2026-09-09. `src/vectors.zig` reproduces
the W3C Web Authentication Level 3 specification's own §16 "Test Vectors"
verbatim, and the W3C licence those come under asks that its notice travel with
them.

Until this revision the module had no NOTICE at all — while reproducing the
material of the same rights holder that `modules/tracecontext` carries a full
attribution for. Two modules, one W3C, opposite treatments; this is the one
that had nothing.

⚠ AND IT IS A DIFFERENT W3C LICENCE FROM `tracecontext`'s, which is the reason
this file does not simply copy that one. `tracecontext`'s vectors come from the
`w3c/trace-context` TEST SUITE, and that repository's own `LICENSE.md` splits
the two cases: "All Reports in this Repository are licensed by contributors
under the W3C Software and Document License … All tests in this Repository are
licensed by contributors to be distributed under the W3C 3-clause BSD License."
The vectors here are not from a test suite — they are read out of the
specification document itself, which is a Report. So the applicable grant is
the **W3C Software and Document License**, not the 3-clause BSD.

Test vectors
------------

`src/vectors.zig` reproduces the byte-exact vectors of W3C Web Authentication
(WebAuthn) Level 3, §16 "Test Vectors"
(https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/#sctn-test-vectors — non-normative, but the
specification's own official conformance vectors). Fetched 2026-07-21 from
https://www.w3.org/TR/webauthn-3/ and extracted mechanically by an offline
Python script (HTML tag-strip plus a regex over the `name = h'…'` CDDL literals
the spec uses, plus a byte-level scan to pull each registration vector's
`credentialPublicKey` out of its own `authData`, which the prose does not give
as a separate named literal).

The extraction is mechanical on purpose: an earlier hand-copy of these vectors
put one signature substring into the wrong test case, and regenerating straight
from the spec text makes that class of error impossible.

W3C notice, retained
--------------------

  Copyright © World Wide Web Consortium. All Rights Reserved. This work is
  distributed under the W3C Software and Document License
  (https://www.w3.org/copyright/software-license/).

The licence's conditions on redistribution are that the copyright notice and
the licence reference travel with the material, and that any modification be
identified as such. This module reproduces the vectors' VALUES as Zig byte-array
declarations rather than the specification's HTML/CDDL text; nothing of the
document's prose is reproduced, and no vector's bytes are altered.

⚠ Stated rather than left implicit: the copyright line above carries no year.
The specification's own status section names one, and it was not re-fetched for
this pass — the notice is reproduced in the form the licence requires, and the
year belongs here once someone re-reads the document header.

**Copyleft:** NONE-SHIPPED — the W3C Software and Document License is
permissive: it asks that the notice travel with the material and imposes no
reciprocity, and no GPL/LGPL/AGPL source or data is present in this module.

